Chapter: Pr87Direct
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 The CONTROL for finding 56. `probe-pr87-alias.codex` compiles when it
 was predicted to refuse, and the conclusion drawn from that -- the
 let-bound alias is what stops the checker asking -- rests on the
 Cobblestone lane's arm A refusing, which was measured on their tree and
 not on ours.

 This is the same definition with the alias removed. One variable
 changed.

 PREDICTION: CDX2001, Integer against a function type. If this ALSO
 compiles then the alias is not the trigger, finding 56 is misattributed,
 and what we have is a plain return-type check that does not run.

Section: Functions

  fx : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  fx (x) (y) = fx x

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni (show (fx 1 2))
  end
